Fixed per-row database queries when rendering custom relationship columns in list views (for example `Device`, `VLAN`, and Virtual Chassis member tables): each row no longer re-fetches the `Relationship` of every association (compared by ID instead), and the `source`/`destination` peers of each association are now batch-prefetched alongside the associations themselves. If a relationship involving the model references a stale content type (an uninstalled App's model), the peer prefetch is skipped and such peers fall back to per-row resolution, rendering as "(unknown)" as before.
